   129	stage) before any pod. Order: the instrumentation is validated on the registered headline cells before the pod; the
   130	diagnostics of the 18 new D2 winners and their reverse switches run on the Mac after the pod's records are retrieved.
   131	Construction: a D2 winner is embedded in D2+H3 by adding `x` (0 for itself, 1 for the reverse switch); each switch is
   132	the mean difference of normalised profits on the evaluation seeds, the reference cancelling. Resets are the focal
   133	provider's identities of generation 1 or more; ban rounds are the ban lengths imposed on its identities; rounds without
   134	an offer are counted separately. Saved per policy: the seed identifiers, the per-seed normalised profits, the per-seed switch differences, and the
   135	reset and ban counts per episode; a D2 winner with any reset stops the run. Spot check: `fresh0@rho0.2|F111` is also
   136	diagnosed on the pod (`--diag-cells`); the Mac's reset and ban counts must equal the pod's exactly, and its numerical
