   171	
   172	Expectations: on all six fresh markets (each market counted; a single market against it fails the expectation), I(B3) > I(R3) and I(C*) > I(R3); pooled S defined and greater than 0.5. Expectations are
   173	scored on point estimates (this is a descriptive follow-up; "met" does not mean that an interval excludes the threshold),
   174	with the denominator gate of section 5 applied separately to the base and the doubled results. Each expectation is
   175	scored as met, failed, or not established: **met** if it holds under both the base and the doubled searches; **failed** if
   176	it fails under both; **not established (search-sensitive)** if the two disagree. An undefined S and a missing cell are
   177	reported as such, separately from failures. A failure is not read as evidence for any particular cause (search error and
   178	mixed outcomes are possible). Only if the pooled-S expectation is met may the paper say: within the D2 family, at the
   179	fixed parameters and search budgets, most of the estimated B3 - R3 gap under the prescribed searches disappears when the
   180	attacker cannot replace its identity.
   181	
   182	## 7. Cost
   183	
   184	**Work.** Measured benchmark (`experiments/v2/benchmark/timings.json`): one unit = a headline D2+H3 cell, 0.579
   185	core-hours. Per D2 cell: 1 unit + 160 further seeds (0.046) + doubling with held-out evaluation (0.479); 18 cells = 27.45
   186	units. Diagnostics: 63 instrumented evaluations + up to 42 switch evaluations = up to 105 single-policy evaluations of
   187	200 episodes, priced conservatively at the profit-evaluation stage's cost for 200 seeds (0.058 units each, although that
   188	stage evaluates more than one profile) = about 6.1 units. Total about 33.6 units = **about 19.4 core-hours**. Draft 5
   189	moves the diagnostics to the Mac (free) and adds the pod gate (about 0.34 USD); the pod estimate below is kept as an
   190	upper bound.
   191	
   192	**Billed pod time.** One 16-vCPU pod at the recorded 0.56 USD per hour; searches with 16 workers, evaluation, doubling,
   193	and diagnostics with at most 10 (operations ledger). Stage schedule with incomplete worker batches and equal benchmark
   194	task times: searches, evaluation, and doubling about 1.77 hours (internal review's computation); diagnostics about 0.6
   195	hours (105 evaluations in batches of 10); preparation 0.3 hours; idle tail 0.3 hours = **about 3.0 billed hours, about
   196	1.66 USD**. The benchmark's unit price (0.0625 USD per unit, at its 0.108 USD per core-hour) gives about 2.10 USD; the plan
   197	uses the larger.
   198	
   199	| Item | Estimate | Cap |
   200	|---|---:|---:|
   201	| Option A: 18 D2 cells, doubling checks, diagnostics | 1.66 to 2.10 USD | **10.00 USD** (author, 2026-11-09) |
   202	
   203	A failed attempt counts toward the cap; the cap leaves room for one early failure, not for a full second run. Option B (an X7-SC variant with replacement disabled) is dropped from this plan: its
   204	constrained family, incumbents, and corner controls would need their own specification (the frozen X7-SC search inserts
   205	D2+H3 incumbents that can replace), so it is not offered for approval.
   206	
   207	**Budget.** `docs/revision/budget-ledger.json`: spent 50.869 USD of the 55 USD approval limit. The author approved option A
   208	on the board on 2026-11-09 and set the cap to 10 USD ("make the cap $10 to ensure we're not blocked by a low cap"). The
   209	ledger needs a new category `followup` with cap 10.00 and the approval limit raised to 61 USD (50.869 + 10 = 60.869,
   210	`python3 -c "print(50.869+10)"`). `scripts/budget_v2.py` is frozen, so the tested wrapper
   211	`docs/revision/followup/budget_followup.py --approve 61 10 TEXT` records both, refuses a limit below spend plus the cap,
   212	and keeps the earlier approval text. The estimate is unchanged (1.66 to 2.10 USD); the higher cap only prevents a stop from a low
   213	cap. Stop at the cap.
   214	
   215	## 8. Steps
   216	
   217	1. Internal review of this plan to consensus; freeze it (commit).
   218	2. Decision card: approved on 2026-11-09, cap 10 USD (card `touchstone-reset-spend`).
   219	3. On approval: write and test the driver (TDD); on the Mac (free), validations (a), (b) and (d) must pass through the
   220	   corrected paths (preflight run, record with provenance and dependency hashes, `gate.json` and an inventory saved in a
   221	   new directory each: `results/v2/followup-repro-v2`, `results/v2/followup-repro-doubling-v2`); earlier passes on the
   222	   older path do not count and the diagnostics are validated on the registered headline
   223	   cells, all before any pod is created.
   224	4. One pod: the reproduction gate first (draft-5 criterion; stop and report on failure), then `--stage all` with
   225	   `--diag-cells fresh0@rho0.2|F111|D2|profit` (inputs, search, freeze, evaluate, doubling, spot diagnostics, inventory);
   226	   records retrieved, the pod deleted and the deletion verified, the spend recorded.
   227	5. On the Mac after retrieval: the diagnostics of all 18 D2 winners and their reverse switches (`--stage diagnostics`),
   228	   checked against the pod's spot-check cell. The three headline cells (registered D2 records) run on the Mac before the
   229	   pod (`--headline-diagnostics`, 200 seeds); with the 18 fresh cells this gives the 63 policies and 42 switch
   230	   comparisons of section 4 plus the 21 reverse switches.
   231	6. Analysis: a new `reset` block in `posthoc_v2.py` (tested first), a table, and a paragraph in section 9 with sites; the
   232	   section-1 headline numbers enter at the same time, labelled exploratory.
   233	7. Internal review of the paper change, then the next external package.
